#: Readme_OMP.md:1
msgid "Threading: openMP"
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:24
msgid ""
"This is nearly identical to the serial version. With few differences: We are"
" asking the system if we want to run with more threads with `unsigned nt = "
"OpenMP::getNumThreads()`, (if is the first time that it is called stores and"
" return the number in the environmental variable `PLUMED_NUM_THREADS`, "
"otherwise it will return the stored number)."
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:27
msgid ""
"Then with that information we open a parallel environment with `#pragma omp "
"parallel num_threads(nt)` in which we explicilty specify the number of "
"threads (otherwise il will use the number in the environmntal variable "
"`OMP_NUM_THREADS`). Note that the pragma is prepended to a scope delimited "
"by curly braces: the code within them will be distribuited between the "
"threads."
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:30
msgid ""
"Then we have the next pragma instruction: `#pragma omp for`: this pragma "
"will tranform the `for` in order to make it work in the multithreaded "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:33
msgid "SPOILER"
msgstr "解答を含む内容"

#: Readme_OMP.md:35
msgid "There is at least a race condition here: can you spot it?"
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:38
msgid "ANSWER"
msgstr "解答"

#: Readme_OMP.md:40
msgid ""
"`ncoord` is the race condition: each time two threads or more threads "
"execute the `+=` simultaneusly they will increment the `ncoord` from the "
"same value, meaning the the number saved in memory has been incremented only"
" once instead of twice or more."
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:42
msgid ""
"The solution is to append `reduction(+:)` to for pragma: `#pragma for "
"reduction(+:)`"
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:46
msgid "Plumed tools used:"
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:47
msgid ""
"`tools/OpenMP.h` contains some function that are useful in working with "
"openMP."
msgstr ""

#: Readme_OMP.md:48
msgid ""
"`OpenMP::getNumThreads()` to get the number of threads from the "
"environmental variable `PLUMED_NUM_THREADS"
msgstr ""

